{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-012-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/ZoneRenderingTests.cs","line":237,"method":"ShouldForceWatchProtectedFullFidelity_OrbitTail_ReturnsFalse","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.WarpLoopPolicy.cs:167; change the body to isWatchProtectedRecording || !isOrbitTailPlayback -> red","what_it_asserts":"ShouldForceWatchProtectedFullFidelity returns false for the pair (isWatchProtectedRecording true, isOrbitTailPlayback true).","why_weak":"A two-boolean predicate with only one of four input pairs asserted, and it is a false-returning pair, so stubbing the method to return false keeps it green. The load-bearing arm (watch-protected non-orbit-tail debris must stay full fidelity, the Issue316 behaviour) is asserted nowhere in Source/Parsek.Tests or Source/Parsek/InGameTests.","proposed_action":"Convert to a Theory over all four (isWatchProtectedRecording, isOrbitTailPlayback) pairs with the expected result, so the true arm is pinned.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-012-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/ZoneRenderingTests.cs","line":245,"method":"ShouldAllowWarpZoneHideExemption_WatchProtectedOrbitTail_ReturnsFalse","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.WarpLoopPolicy.cs:161; change the body to !(isWatchProtectedRecording || isOrbitTailPlayback) -> red","what_it_asserts":"ShouldAllowWarpZoneHideExemption returns false for the pair (true, true).","why_weak":"The predicate is !(a && b), so three of four input pairs return true and none of them is asserted anywhere in the suite; stubbing the method to return false keeps this test green. The suppressed case is the only one pinned, so a regression that stops allowing the exemption for ordinary warping orbital ghosts stays silent.","proposed_action":"Convert to a Theory over all four pairs with the expected result, mirroring the companion ShouldForceWatchProtectedFullFidelity change.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-012-03","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/ZoneRenderingTests.cs","line":479,"method":"ApplyWatchedFullFidelityOverride_Forced_ClearsAllSuppression","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.cs:8658; change the forced return to (shouldHideMesh, false, false) -> red","what_it_asserts":"With forceFullFidelity true, an all-true suppression triple is cleared to all false.","why_weak":"Only the forced arm is asserted in this file. The pass-through arm (force false must return the input triple unchanged) is what keeps distance LOD working for unwatched ghosts, and nothing here would red if it started clearing suppression unconditionally.","proposed_action":"Add the force=false case asserting the (true, true, true) input triple comes back unchanged.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
